    switch clock: S/zeta = -5.005e-01, beta_iso = 2.003e-01  (FAIL)
    -> a switch keyed to the local temperature or to local proper time is adiabatic (S = 0): in the growing mode both are
       the same local clock. Isocurvature appears only for a trigger with its OWN fluctuation (a spectator clock):
       S = (1/2) d ln t_i per unit, so beta_iso <= 0.02 needs |d tau / t_i| <= 0.29 zeta. CORRECTION to the frozen hand
       expectation 'S-t EXCLUDED': a global-time switch is not excluded unless its clock fluctuates independently.

